      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "5fd8430f6249ae2fb1ef2f3c",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "There is a slight performance cost to this (plus the gotcha of not noticing it is an issue), so it is preferable for this to be fixed by the devs, but in the meantime, here is a solution I implemented.\nHave the event also set a boolean to true as soon as the event was raised, and subsequent calls to the event will not perform any action if that bool is true.\nThen in the Update() method, I have a timer that starts counting time since the boolean was set to true, and once that time reaches 2.5 seconds, the boolean is set back to false.\nI also disable the box collider for the chair until the timer elapses, so that someone can't immediately get back into the chair before the timer has fully elapsed.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
